          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9203504d7a0874043e3ef04f54e8b411538f0adda46fb493fdaa79831de452be:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5ea3a5940a7048d48e32ee631550343e",
      "statement": "Per-user bring-your-own provider credentials are explicitly out of scope for ADR-0001: they remain per-run and BFF-encrypted, are never centralized into Komodo or Vault, and a request lacking a per-user credential fails closed with no shared-secret fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/ADR-0001-prod-secrets-management.md#L68-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81c37890573869b8783252990ff0675917453c5b2338459b3b5afae02c978b04:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9754624b0674e6d8dcd436e8011db47",
      "statement": "Rotation under ADR-0001 is manual by design (edit the Komodo Variable and redeploy the affected stack); automated rotation, lease/TTL, and fine-grained secret-access audit are explicit non-goals until the ADR's §7 revisit trigger fires (dynamic short-lived DB credentials wanted, mandated rotation/audit becomes required, or the footprint grows to multiple hosts or operators).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/ADR-0001-prod-secrets-management.md#L64-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b356bb556765f8cb0ce7ea8f15e3348f00dee3bb8cf677bcbe6f1b665f51bcc8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84eb14e14fe9494d95f710e1ea845d11",
      "statement": "The seven core production stacks (prod-auth, prod-mc-service, prod-mcm-bff, prod-movie-assistant, prod-audit, prod-observability, prod-vault) are declared as [[stack]] blocks in infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml, each carrying env_file_path = \".env.prod\"; six of them also declare an environment block whose secret-bearing values are masked [[Variable]] tokens, so the committed TOML carries only tokens and never a secret value, while prod-vault is the one stack with no environment block because it holds no secret to interpolate. prod-auth is the only block that also carries a non-secret literal in its environment block (PROD_REALM_FILE=/home/prod/keycloak/prod-realm.rendered.json), so \"masked tokens only\" applies to secret-bearing values rather than to every line.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml#L128-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47a5beb8b1258bc79670195e27a56d2344c8b1495f5d2d133bd7942a9f28b9aa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml#L26-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e701370b00fb6772909c7b6d8e0ca19fa2ff90f063872c1cd9fc30cce35b1fef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e0164b04cf74da8b0986146079e53a3",
      "statement": "Because Komodo writes a stack's environment block into that stack's env_file_path, adding a required ${VAR:?} reference to a prod compose is a change to that stack's declared inputs in stacks.toml; the break is invisible in CI (the compose files are valid and the dev stack supplies the value from its own generated env file) and only surfaces on a real Komodo deploy, which is why scripts/__tests__/komodo-stack-env.guard.test.mjs asserts every required variable a prod compose declares is supplied by its Komodo stack.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml#L1-L24",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b062bd22ea6fcd113b5247c363812c1cef3c61ef9d0213d345a0dac0e6c03e8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/__tests__/komodo-stack-env.guard.test.mjs#L1-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37198a3514ad1bc298281e0924a3218c795c73cbdad9983333d89e1dba1b3f32:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_08abb6ebe7034c6e8966b543fb0a91d0",
      "statement": "prod-vault is the Komodo stack that declares no secret at all: it runs a real (non-dev) Vault on raft storage uninitialized and sealed with no root token in environment, and overrides its healthcheck status codes so Komodo reads the intentionally dormant server as healthy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/vault/compose.prod.yaml#L1-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d932545d01b8415239c9c4f998ce517e0ee2e4b7d3c0deecfb907bc570d35852:"
