    {
      "id": "claim_27e99a02f0c8460b90a73e18cafdd820",
      "statement": "The komodo-stack-env guard's scope is deliberately narrow and mechanical: it counts a stack's `additional_env_files` (e.g. the committed `.env.deploy` digests) as supplying a variable, matches only the fail-fast `${VAR:?}` form and not optional `${VAR}`/`${VAR:-default}` tunables, strips comment lines before scanning so documented examples like `${VAR:?example}` are not counted, and skips a `file_paths` entry that does not exist on disk; a separate test proves the guard is not vacuously green by deleting LANGFUSE_RUSTFS_SECRET_KEY from a copy of stacks.toml and asserting the parser no longer reports it supplied while the observability prod compose still requires it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/__tests__/komodo-stack-env.guard.test.mjs#L25-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c1e4b8cdd5c592ec08cfef092daa27de48da5c53287932cadd840663f25f5f6f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ab922369cf8b479fbe6b19fa2404010b",
      "statement": "The guard test's own header records the two live, opposite-direction instances of the declared-inputs coupling: feature 069 repointed the observability object store at the repository's own build, making prod-observability the fourth consumer of REGISTRY_HOST while stacks.toml declared it only for the other three, and the real Komodo deploy failed on `required variable REGISTRY_HOST is missing a value`; feature 080 then moved that image back to upstream RustFS, which removed REGISTRY_HOST from the block and added LANGFUSE_RUSTFS_SECRET_KEY, and the guard went red on the new variable until stacks.toml declared it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/__tests__/komodo-stack-env.guard.test.mjs#L1-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9902f72fae1da2aecc37bccd2791140144d49f64c689128fef4d4082218fe433:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_aea7de8273204b87a4bec1cc65512a02",
      "statement": "The guard only proves the direction \"every required variable is supplied\": it cannot detect a declared input no compose reads any more, and the `environment` block is a hand-maintained declared-input list, so an entry can outlive its consumer. KC_ADMIN_BIND_IP was dropped from the keycloak compose bind by feature 028 and from prod-auth's block on 2026-10-12, TS_ADMIN_IP followed on 2026-10-13, and feature 080 deliberately leaves REGISTRY_HOST and LANGFUSE_MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD seeded in Komodo until the object-store rollback window closes because reverting that change restores the lines that reference them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/prod-reboot-resilience.md#L98-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25010e416df6366df3bf6e96792aa88a14f91e17bb36ffc89adef8bf364b39f3:"
        },
